    "https://osumarion.osu.edu/about-us/student-advisory-board": {
      "title": "Dean’s Student Advisory Board",
      "description": "Dean’s Student Advisory Board | The Ohio State University at Marion Skip to main content Show Links OSU.edu Buckeye Link Map Webmail Search Ohio State Future Students Admissions Contact Us Financial Aid Housing Majors and Programs Regional Campus Commitment Program Orientation Meet the Support Services Team Parent and Family Resources Resources for Admitted Buckeyes Visit Current Students Academic Support Services Bookstore Buckeyes First Career Services Counseling & Wellness Services Dining Services Financial Aid First Year Experience Health Insurance Housing On-Campus Student Job Opportunities STEP Program Student Life Campus Recreation Discount and Giveaway Donation Form FAQ Policies Student ID Campus Safety Dining Services Homecoming Housing Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Student Opportunity Development Fund Student Success Programming Information for Students Alumni Alumni Hall of Fame Buckeye Backers Delaware Alumni Club Marion Alumni Club Ohio State Alumni Association Transcripts Outreach About Us Dean’s Student Advisory Board External Event Reservations Ohio State Marion Board Community Outreach AI for the Community Buckeye Talks on Tap Build Your Own Prairie The Downtown Engagement Hub Larry R. Yoder Prairie Learning Laboratory Pelotonia Team Marion Ralph W. Howard Service Award Warren G. Harding Symposium Cultural Arts Five Nights on Campus Kuhn Fine Art Gallery The Art of the Pair Educational Partnerships GoBuck$ Pay It Forward Pride & Life Skills Mentoring Program 60 Robotics Competition Teacher Manufacturing Boot Camp Youth Programs Academics Academic Calendar Academic Majors & Programs Associate of Arts Degree Biology Biology Majors & Minors Center for Life Sciences Education Major Requirements Resources & Opportunities Summer Programs Biology News Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Engineering Technology Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Dean’s Student Advisory Board Dean’s Student Advisory Board Dean’s Student Advisory Board Dean’s Student Advisory Board is charged with advising the Ohio State Marion Dean on matters that shape the student experience, including academics, communication, campus life, engagement opportunities, and the overall quality of the Marion student experience. As a regional campus, Ohio State Marion offers a close-knit community where students, faculty, and staff interact more directly and frequently. The Board helps ensure student voices are heard in real time and that campus decisions reflect the unique strengths, needs, and opportunities of a smaller campus environment—supporting student success, belonging, and connection to both Marion and the broader The Ohio State University community. Board Membership Board membership consists of a cross-sectional group of undergraduate students representing different majors, class years, and levels of campus involvement. Members are invited to serve to ensure the Board reflects diverse student perspectives, experiences, and pathways—including students preparing to campus-change and those planning to complete their degree at Marion. The Board is advisory in nature and is designed to foster open, constructive dialogue between students and campus leadership. Members are expected to share both personal experiences and broader trends they observe among their peers . Dean’s Student Advisory Board 2026–2027 We extend our sincere thanks to the students who serve on the Dean’s Student Advisory Board for the 2025–2026 academic year and contribute thoughtful insights on the student experience at Ohio State Marion. Members: Liv Frazier, Senior, Psychology & Criminology Katie Tibbals, Junior, Psychology Gavin Westendorf, Sophomore , Engineering Technolog y Katy Beck, Junior, Psychology Simon Kubelik, Sophomore, Chemistry Ansh Sidhu, Sophomore, Biology Jacob Duke, Senior, History, minoring in Design Thinking 2026-2027 Meetings All meetings are held from 12:40pm-1:40pm in Maynard Hall 230, Bull Board Room Autumn Semester September 21 October 22 November 16 December 14 Spring Semester January 14 February 15 March 15 April 19 Serving on the Board Each year, the Dean Schlueter invites students to serve on the Dean’s Student Advisory Board. Students may be asked to complete a brief interest form and/or participate in a short conversation to support the creation of a balanced and representative Board. The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, please contact us . Privacy Statement Non-discrimination Notice Cookie Settings Site Map © 2026 The Ohio State University Back to top"
    },
    "https://osumarion.osu.edu/engineering/career-opportunities-engineering": {
      "title": "Academics",
      "description": "Engineering | The Ohio State University at Marion Skip to main content Show Links OSU.edu Buckeye Link Map Webmail Search Ohio State Future Students Admissions Contact Us Financial Aid Housing Majors and Programs Regional Campus Commitment Program Orientation Meet the Support Services Team Parent and Family Resources Resources for Admitted Buckeyes Visit Current Students Academic Support Services Bookstore Buckeyes First Career Services Counseling & Wellness Services Dining Services Financial Aid First Year Experience Health Insurance Housing On-Campus Student Job Opportunities STEP Program Student Life Campus Recreation Discount and Giveaway Donation Form FAQ Policies Student ID Campus Safety Dining Services Homecoming Housing Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Student Opportunity Development Fund Student Success Programming Information for Students Alumni Alumni Hall of Fame Buckeye Backers Delaware Alumni Club Marion Alumni Club Ohio State Alumni Association Transcripts Outreach About Us Dean’s Student Advisory Board External Event Reservations Ohio State Marion Board Community Outreach AI for the Community Buckeye Talks on Tap Build Your Own Prairie The Downtown Engagement Hub Larry R. Yoder Prairie Learning Laboratory Pelotonia Team Marion Ralph W. Howard Service Award Warren G. Harding Symposium Cultural Arts Five Nights on Campus Kuhn Fine Art Gallery The Art of the Pair Educational Partnerships GoBuck$ Pay It Forward Pride & Life Skills Mentoring Program 60 Robotics Competition Teacher Manufacturing Boot Camp Youth Programs Academics Academic Calendar Academic Majors & Programs Associate of Arts Degree Biology Biology Majors & Minors Center for Life Sciences Education Major Requirements Resources & Opportunities Summer Programs Biology News Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Engineering Technology Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Engineering Career Opportunities In Engineering Academics Honors & Undergrad Research Summer Semester Academic Support Services Academic Majors & Programs Sociology/Criminology Leadership Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News Associate of Arts Degree Engineering Technology Social Work Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News Biology Study Abroad Course Guide Library Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Cancelled Classes Campus Resource Guide Academic Calendar Academic Recognition Awards Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering refers to any type of science concerned with the design, construction and use of machines, systems and structures. It's a vast field that has applications in nearly every industry, from manufacturing and production to shipping and construction. Engineers of various types were likely involved in the home you live in, the building you work at, the bridges you drive over and the products that you buy. If you’re interested in problem solving, experimentation and machine development, a career in engineering may suit you. What are the 5 main engineering fields Engineering is one of the broadest fields of study, and the exact skills and duties of an engineer can vary depending on the field they specialize in. Some of the main types of engineering fields include Chemical engineering Civil engineering Computer science engineering Electrical engineering Mechanical engineering Popular careers in engineering (from Indeed.com) If you’re interested in a career in engineering, you’ll find that there are many specialties to explore. Below are 14 common types of engineering careers you might consider: aeronautical engineer, biomedical engineer, chemical engineer, civil engineer, computer science engineer, electrical engineer, environmental engineer. industrial engineer, marine engineer, materials engineer, mechanical engineer, nuclear engineer, petroleum engineer, and software engineer. Engineering is salaries in these fields range on average from $74,000 to $130,000 annually. Engineering is considered one of the more lucrative career fields to enter. Campus Involvement in Engineering Ohio State Marion offers a world-class engineering technology education in a personalized and cost-effective learning environment. Students receive hands-on lab experiences in our state-of the-art facilities and have the opportunity to participate in undergraduate research. In addition, Ohio State Marion partners with regional manufacturers to offer immersive and applicable internship and senior capstone experiences. Engineering students can also join student chapters of nationally-recognized industry organizations including the Society of Manufacturing Engineers, the National Society of Professional Engineers or the Society of Women Engineers. Internships and co-ops at Ohio State Marion Engineering students at Ohio State Marion have access to internships through the Office of Engineering Career Services (ecs.osu.edu). Students have recently obtained internships with Anderson Windows, Fidelity, Whirlpool, ArcelorMittal Tubular, Sakamura Machine Co., LTD., and others. Requirements for applying to the Internship and Co-op program include completing at least 1.5 semesters at Ohio State and maintaining a GPA of at least 2.5. Interested in applying for internships? Students may also utilize Handshake , Ohio State's new university-wide position posting system where students have access to search and apply for part-time jobs, internships, co-ops, and full-time career opportunities. Thousands of jobs, internship and career opportunities are posted in Handshake as well as information on upcoming career fairs and on-campus recruiting events. The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, please contact us . Privacy Statement Non-discrimination Notice Cookie Settings Site Map © 2026 The Ohio State University Back to top"
    },
    "https://osumarion.osu.edu/psychology/careers": {
      "title": "Careers in Psychology",
      "description": "Careers in Psychology | The Ohio State University at Marion Skip to main content Show Links OSU.edu Buckeye Link Map Webmail Search Ohio State Future Students Admissions Contact Us Financial Aid Housing Majors and Programs Regional Campus Commitment Program Orientation Meet the Support Services Team Parent and Family Resources Resources for Admitted Buckeyes Visit Current Students Academic Support Services Bookstore Buckeyes First Career Services Counseling & Wellness Services Dining Services Financial Aid First Year Experience Health Insurance Housing On-Campus Student Job Opportunities STEP Program Student Life Campus Recreation Discount and Giveaway Donation Form FAQ Policies Student ID Campus Safety Dining Services Homecoming Housing Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Student Opportunity Development Fund Student Success Programming Information for Students Alumni Alumni Hall of Fame Buckeye Backers Delaware Alumni Club Marion Alumni Club Ohio State Alumni Association Transcripts Outreach About Us Dean’s Student Advisory Board External Event Reservations Ohio State Marion Board Community Outreach AI for the Community Buckeye Talks on Tap Build Your Own Prairie The Downtown Engagement Hub Larry R. Yoder Prairie Learning Laboratory Pelotonia Team Marion Ralph W. Howard Service Award Warren G. Harding Symposium Cultural Arts Five Nights on Campus Kuhn Fine Art Gallery The Art of the Pair Educational Partnerships GoBuck$ Pay It Forward Pride & Life Skills Mentoring Program 60 Robotics Competition Teacher Manufacturing Boot Camp Youth Programs Academics Academic Calendar Academic Majors & Programs Associate of Arts Degree Biology Biology Majors & Minors Center for Life Sciences Education Major Requirements Resources & Opportunities Summer Programs Biology News Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Engineering Technology Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Psychology Careers In Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology is the scientific study of the mind and behavior. Psychologists are actively involved in studying and understanding mental processes, brain functions, and behavior. The field of psychology is considered a \"Hub Science\" with strong connections to the medical sciences, social sciences, and education (Boyack, Klavans, & Borner, 2005). An education in psychology provides students with valuable skills employers seek, such as critical thinking and problem solving (Kuther, 2013). Because psychology connects with so many different areas, psychology majors are well-positioned to pursue careers in many different areas. Individuals with a Bachelor’s degree in psychology are employed in 92 different occupation categories (American Psychological Association Center for Workforce Studies, 2017). Below you'll find some of the job categories, specific job titles, and some Ohio State Marion alumni who are employed in those areas. Education/Advising Trestin Weikle (2017) School Psychologist London City Schools School counselors help students succeed in school and plan their career. They help students form healthy goals, mindsets and behaviors, learn to develop effective collaboration and cooperation skills, to practice perseverance, to develop time management and study skills, and to learn selfmotivation and self-direction habits. Job Titles: Academic Advisor Admissions Counselor Camp Counselor/ Coordinator Consultant Elementary School Manager Head Aftercare Teacher In Home Autism Instructor Intensive Early Intervention Interpretive Aide Lead Preschool Teacher Middle School Program Coordinator Operations Coordinator Para Educator Post-baccalaureate Teaching Assistant Preschool Teacher Program Excellence Associate Teaching Assistant Youth Development Specialist Healthcare Amy Ware (2007) Healthcare Admin James Cancer Hospital Healthcare administrators direct the operation of healthcare organizations and rarely meet directly with the patients in the healthcare facility. They shape the policy that runs the facility and improve the patients’ experience. Job Titles: Dental Assistant Drug Safety Associate EMT Home Health Aide Lab Manager Laboratory Technician Medical and Research Assistant Medical Scribe Mental Health Associate/Technician Orthopedic Receptionist Pharmacy Technician Protege Intern of Recovery and Care Public Health Analyst Trainee Business | Management | Marketing Kori Montgomery (2016) Office Manager Office of Student Life, The Ohio State University A Business Manager, or Office Manager, is responsible for overseeing business operations across departments. Their duties include hiring new staff, conducting office meetings and coming up with proactive strategies to improve productivity and employee morale. Job Titles: Account Executive/Management Analyst Associate District Manager Brand Associate Business Analyst Campus Project Specialist CASE Fundraising Intern Client Service Analyst Consultant District Manager Junior Negotiator Legal Assistant Loan Officer Assistant Management Consulting Analyst Marketplace Integrity Agent Mathematical Statistician Paralegal Production Assistant Quality Assurance Specialist Residential Real Estate Agent Sales Associate Securities Analyst SEO Specialist Store Management Executive Strategic Operations Analyst Travel Specialist Human Services | Therapy CheyAnne Mullins (2015) Caseworker Crawford County Jobs & Family Services Child welfare caseworkers are usually social workers who work with children and families to promote and protect the welfare of children. Child, family, and school social workers work for government agencies, schools, social service agencies, residential care facilities and hospitals. Their responsibilities and job duties include monitoring a child's progress at home and at school, ensuring that a child has adequate shelter and nourishment, helping families access social services and intervening in hostile family situations. Job Titles: ABA Therapist/Instructor Associate Behavioral Therapist Behavior Therapist Behavioral Health Technician Behavioral Technician Community Psychiatric Supportive Therapist Intake Coordinator Program Aide Program Manager Registered Behavior Therapist Rehab/Recovery Counselor Rehabilitation Counselor RISE Intern Senior Neuropsychology Intern Supported Employment Specialist Treatment Coordinator Therapeutic Mentor Human Resources/IO Nathan Baker (2020) Pursuing Ph.D. in I/O Psychology Michigan State University I/O Psychologists study individual behavior in the work setting; selection, placement, training, and development of employees; performance evaluation; job satisfaction and quality of work life; promote organizational development Job Titles: Corporate Recruiter Engagement Associate Human Resource Generalist/Analyst Human Resources Analyst Human Resources Coordinator Job Placement Specialist Leadership Consultant National Recruitment Coordinator Recruiter Recruiter, Accounting and Finance Recruitment Consultant- Microsoft Cloud Technologies Staffing Coordinator Technical Analyst/Recruiter Research Emily Meadows (2013) Research Assistant Nationwide Children's Hospital Pursuing Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology, University of Toledo Researchers work in almost every industry and are hired to recognize patterns and locate, analyze, and interpret data. They work in fields including academia, science, medicine, finance, and other sectors. Researchers analyze and interpret patterns and trends and record findings through written notes and appropriate software. They conduct desktop research and using books, journal articles, newspaper sources, questionnaires, surveys, and interviews. They maintain and protect electronic databases, write proposals, and deliver presentations. Job Titles: Clinical Research Assistant Clinical Study Coordinator Environmental Justice Researcher Faculty Research Assistant/Staff Intramural Research Training Award (Research Assistant Fellow) IRTA Lab Manager MRI Participant Navigator Research and Recruitment Coordinator Research Assistant Research Coordinator/Project Manager (Faculty Assistant) Research Project Assistant Summer Post-Bac, Research The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, please contact us . Privacy Statement Non-discrimination Notice Cookie Settings Site Map © 2026 The Ohio State University Back to top"
